{
  "$comment": [
    "spells_us.txt FIELD CHECKS, shared by the app (src/main/resist/spellsUsSemantics.ts) and the engine (engine/crates/fold/src/spells_us/layout.rs, include_str!). Each check runs over the REALIGNED rows; a file passes when every check passes on at least `floor` of them. `measured` is each check's share on the owner's install (2026-11-25, 74,024 rows): `real` aligned, `left`/`right` when the column reads c-1/c+1 (what a one-column move does), `prefixMin` the lowest share over the first 1k, 2k, 3k, 5k, 8k, 12k, 20k, 37k and 60k rows (a file a patcher is still writing).",
    "WHICH CHECKS: one is kept only if a shifted share falls well under its real share. Interior class columns 37..50, the runs 16-17, 20-21, 24-25, 34 and 57..73 are left out: a move cannot change them, so they only add false-alarm risk.",
    "WHERE THE FLOOR SITS: where the highest shifted share at least ten points below the real one is near zero (<= 10%), the floor is that share + 5 points; otherwise the midpoint of the two. A floor never sits above a prefix's share: c55 (21% overall, 2.2% in the first 1,000 rows) is 0.01, and c6, c11, c27 are set by hand under their prefix minima. tests/spellsUsChecksMeasured.test.mts holds every floor between its shifted share and its prefix minimum.",
    "FIELD CHECKS NEED A REAL-SIZED FILE: they are shares over rows, so they run only when the file has at least `minRows` realigned rows. A smaller file is `pending` in the app (a file still being written, never served); the engine judges it on width alone so its few-row test tables still load. Tests that exercise the checks pass a minimum of 0.",
    "FAIL-SAFE BY DESIGN: a move that swaps identical columns (the all-zero run 56..74, the 255 class block) changes no value the parser reads, yet can still fail a neighbouring check and pause the data. That is accepted: a paused estimate is honest, a wrong one is not.",
    "Bump `version` with any change: the app's layout sidecar is keyed on it."
  ],
  "version": 4,
  "minRows": 1000,
